  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 4.4: \"Sensitivity of PTRRα to α on selected LCDB instances (T = 44, k = 22)\". Normalised cumulative reward (ALG/OPT) against α from 0.1 to 1.0, six datasets, each a line with a shaded 95% band. The reading the figure is for is that the datasets DISAGREE about α: ds 55 is flat at about 0.995 throughout, ds 67 RISES with α (0.943 to 0.954), ds 16 peaks in the middle around 0.846 at α≈0.4-0.7, while ds 58 (0.907 to 0.886), ds 19 (0.789 to 0.722) and ds 46 (0.735 to 0.696) all FALL. Every curve's total variation across the sweep is small — the largest, ds 19, moves about 0.067 — so the sensitivity is real but shallow, and the bands of ds 19 and ds 46 overlap over much of the range.",
